.TH CLIPCONNECT 1 "2026" "ClipConnect 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
clipconnect \- automated, encrypted clipboard sync between Android and Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clipconnect
.br
.B clipconnect pair
.br
.B clipconnect unpair
.br
.B clipconnect logs
.br
.B clipconnect help
.br
.B clipconnect version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ClipConnect
syncs the clipboard bidirectionally between an Android phone and a Linux
laptop on the same LAN. Copy text on either device and it appears on the
other within a couple of seconds. Pairing is a one-time QR scan; everything
after that is automatic. Traffic is end-to-end encrypted (AES-256-GCM).
The daemon runs as the normal user under a systemd user unit and never as
root.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B clipconnect
Open the interactive keyboard menu: pair, unpair, view logs, or help.
.TP
.B clipconnect pair
Generate a new pairing secret, open the firewall, restart the daemon, and
show a QR code. Re-pairs unconditionally, revoking previously paired phones.
.TP
.B clipconnect unpair [--yes]
Remove the pairing secret and disconnect. \fB\-\-yes\fR skips the prompt.
.TP
.B clipconnect logs [\fB\-\-follow\fR] [\fB\-\-lines\fR N]
Show daemon logs. Clipboard plaintext and secrets are never logged.
.TP
.B clipconnect help
Show installation, pairing, and troubleshooting help.
.TP
.B clipconnect version
Print the version.
.SH PORT
The daemon listens on TCP \fB10369\fR. \fBufw\fR is opened automatically on
first pair (one sudo prompt).
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.IP X11
\fbxclip\fR or \fbxsel\fR
.IP Wayland (wlroots / KDE)
\fBwl-clipboard\fR (\fBwl-paste\fR / \fBwl-copy\fR)
.IP Android
Allow auto-launch, background running, and "no restrictions" battery for
ClipConnect on OEM skins that kill background apps.
.SH SECURITY
The QR is effectively a password \fBdo not share it.\fR No telemetry, no
analytics, no internet access.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/clipconnect/secret
The pairing secret (mode 0600).
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/clipconnect.service
The systemd user unit.
.SH SEE ALSO
The project README for the full setup and troubleshooting guide.
